# POST /api/customers uniqueness: email and phone are unique across all people after normalization, the email is checked
# first; the 409 carries its reason in `detail` and a refused create leaves no row behind. Names are not unique.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@AdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@AdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@RunId = {{$timestamp}}
@Tag = {{RunId.toString().slice(-8).split('').map(d => 'ABCDEFGHIJ'[d]).join('')}}
@Digits = {{RunId.toString().slice(-7)}}
@BaseEmail = create.conflict.{{RunId}}@example.test

### [Setup][Customers] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Customers] Login as admin (200 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{AdminEmail}}", "password": "{{AdminPassword}}" }

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('__Host-arsm-csrf-token='))?.match(/^__Host-arsm-csrf-token=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Customers] Create the base customer holding the email and the phone (201 expected)
# @name baseCustomer
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Base", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "{{BaseEmail}}", "phoneNumber": "+3670{{Digits}}" }

?? status == 201

###

### [Negative][Customers] The same email again (409 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Second", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "{{BaseEmail}}", "phoneNumber": null }

?? status == 409
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "A person with this email already exists.") == true

###

### [Negative][Customers] The same email in upper case with spaces (409 expected, compared after normalization)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Second", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": " {{BaseEmail.toUpperCase()}} ", "phoneNumber": null }

?? status == 409
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "A person with this email already exists.") == true

###

### [Negative][Customers] The same phone written in national format (409 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Second", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "create.conflict.phone.{{RunId}}@example.test", "phoneNumber": "06 70 {{Digits}}" }

?? status == 409
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "A person with this phone number already exists.") == true

###

### [Negative][Customers] Email and phone both taken (409 expected, the email is reported first)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Second", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "{{BaseEmail}}", "phoneNumber": "+3670{{Digits}}" }

?? status == 409
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "A person with this email already exists.") == true

###

### [Negative][Customers] A mechanic's email is taken too (409 expected, uniqueness spans all people)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Second", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "{{AdminEmail}}", "phoneNumber": null }

?? status == 409
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "A person with this email already exists.") == true

###

### [Positive][Customers] The same names with another email and no phone are fine (201 expected, names are not unique)
# @name twinCustomer
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Base", "middleName": null, "lastName": "Holder-{{Tag}}", "email": "create.conflict.twin.{{RunId}}@example.test", "phoneNumber": null }

?? status == 201

###

### [Positive][Customers] Only the base customer and its twin exist, the refused creates left nothing (200 expected)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers?search={{Tag}}&pageSize=10

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.totalCount == 2

###

### [Cleanup][Customers] Delete the base customer (204 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{baseCustomer.id}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204

###

### [Cleanup][Customers] Delete the twin (204 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{twinCustomer.id}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204
